## STORYBOOK REVIEW POLICY
- Judge the complete editorial composition, not isolated educational figures.
- Backgrounds, textures, quiet page halves, partial characters, ornaments, and illustrations continuing across a gutter are meaningful.
- A paired image spread fails if either physical half is absent, replaced by blank space, independently cropped at the gutter, or enlarged to impersonate both halves.
- Desktop and tablet must preserve genuine facing pages side by side. Reject `max-lg:` stacking that breaks the spread.
- Mobile may stack in DOM order, but the halves must remain visually connected: no repeated page framing, no large artificial gap, and no forced `min-h-[100svh]` on every stacked half.
- Principal artwork must fill the height of its page half on desktop/tablet without distortion. Preserve essential characters, borders, captions, and narrative details.
- A single portrait cover/title page must fit the viewport by height. Reject a full-width portrait rendering that makes the document substantially taller than the viewport.
- Text and verse must never have an internal scrollbar. Reject `overflow-auto`, `overflow-y-*`, clipped text, collisions, or text hidden behind art.
- Prefer reducing decorative padding and stanza gaps when desktop/tablet content can fit one viewport. Mobile may use natural document flow for readability.
- Preserve source alignment, stanza lineation, palette, and visual hierarchy. Do not turn the spread into generic cards or unrelated panels.
- Do not add invented text or images. A missing image leaf may be restored only with its exact supplied `data-id` and `/api/books/{{ label }}/images/IMAGE_ID` source.

