The supplied screenshots are full-page captures. A screenshot substantially taller than its viewport indicates document scrolling and must be justified by readable content, never by forced per-half viewport height or decorative whitespace.

## CORRECTION RULES
- Preserve all `data-id` values, exact text, DOM reading order, and semantic `adt-*` typography classes.
- Elements with a text `data-id` must have literal text children only.
- Keep exactly one top-level section and its `data-section-id`/`data-section-type`.
- Use Tailwind utilities only; no scripts, external styles, or event handlers.
- Use only the responsive prefixes listed above.
- If the current HTML is acceptable, approve it. If correction is possible, return the complete corrected fragment. If a required source asset is unavailable, reject with empty content instead of fabricating it.

## RESPONSE FORMAT
Return `approved`, concise `reasoning`, and `content`. Storybook review does not use textbook crop geometry, so always return `geometry_updates: []` and `transcription_updates: []`.
